From 203d87bcede99c7de7a8744231c076d5a997e922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:26:04 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): LinuxCNC and Tormach probe programs stop before
 G10 L20 when a work offset is rotated

The write G10 L20 P<n> X[#5420-#190] gives "target = active offset +
deviation" (#2610) only for work offsets without an XY rotation. With a
rotation (R of G10 L2, parameter 5210 + 20 x the system number) a target
whose rotation differs gets an origin that is right at the probe position
only, and the public reference does not state what G10 L20 keeps for an
axis without a word.

The post cannot read the rotation, so the program tests it at run time:
before each G10 L20 that writes X or Y, an O-word block tests the rotation
register of the section's work offset and of the target, shows a message
that names them and ends with M2. A Z-only result and a measure-only
result have no test. linuxcnc.cps now keeps the section's offset number.

Pinned by crates/post/tests/probe_rotated_wcs.rs. Six Tormach probe
goldens gain the four guard lines. Decision:
docs/decisions/2683-probe-rotated-wcs.md.

Fixes #2683

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
